@mtrmac, Fair point on the locking, and I can't point at the path.   What I can say is how it was reproduced.  @hayzamjs hit it on 16.x with ZFS during sylve stack creation, which ran one `podman pull` per image in parallel.  I was able to reproduce his error (`chtimes ...: bad file descriptor from ApplyLayer`)  on a slow (overloaded n100) FreeBSD 16.x ZFS box running two copies of this at once: 

`for i in $(seq 20); do podman rmi -f ghcr.io/daemonless/grafana:pkg-latest; podman pull -q ghcr.io/daemonless/grafana:pkg-latest || break; done` 

On a faster host, I haven't been able to reproduce it.
